pe": "concept", "title": "events and sponsorships"}], "description": "Students compare advertising, subscriptions, membership, philanthropy, licensing, events, and platform revenue."}, {"id": "ee13df21-31a5-4e93-aeae-491877819291", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Platform economics", "children": [{"id": "753e2d4e-5eb5-44d6-a4c3-c8e4b77f0aa4", "type": "concept", "title": "platform dependency"}, {"id": "29fa13be-e164-4138-a666-f5cfcde26e2d", "type": "concept", "title": "algorithmic distribution"}, {"id": "1658070d-73da-44c4-ba20-daeca03a4ead", "type": "concept", "title": "creator monetization"}], "description": "Students learn how search engines, social networks, app stores, and video platforms affect traffic and bargaining power."}, {"id": "3b031bda-4c8c-41bc-93ce-87f22fa746d1", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Labor and newsroom change", "children": [{"id": "a2976563-5895-4d8f-bc72-82305e918dc8", "type": "concept", "title": "newsroom jobs"}, {"id": "b82c96b1-a6d8-44cc-bfb5-d5dfd76430d1", "type": "concept", "title": "freelancing"}, {"id": "952a8620-bb0c-46db-b9f7-741713f408ae", "type": "concept", "title": "automation and workflow"}], "description": "The unit covers newsroom roles, freelance work, unions, automation, and changing career pathways."}]}, {"id": "5b30c815-9156-4037-84ed-e969ff5775dd", "type": "topic", "title": "Media Effects, Audiences, and Public Opinion", "description": "This unit introduces evidence-based ways to discuss influence without overstating media power or ignoring audience agency.", "children": [{"id": "71e26c60-9cfd-4321-86c9-250eea89a36a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Effects research basics", "children": [{"id": "49eb9e16-5455-4890-af72-370943a372c6", "type": "concept", "title": "experiments"}, {"id": "18781e24-5706-4b51-8628-da3f6c603a3b", "type": "concept", "title": "surveys"}, {"id": "de6c49c6-5571-4ef1-ac9b-1a2b53e314f3", "type": "concept", "title": "longitudinal research"}], "description": "Students learn the difference between correlation, causation, short-term effects, and long-term social influence."}, {"id": "b2c0e570-9287-4d11-b413-4067ff01ca34", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Public opinion and political communication", "children": [{"id": "c8647170-7a26-416f-be58-6384e2c609e2", "type": "concept", "title": "opinion formation"}, {"id": "cbc00652-e4bc-4ce0-87b5-d7378868955b", "type": "concept", "title": "political ads"}, {"id": "ec905a5d-5271-4cb4-806f-e9f8bc1d4211", "type": "concept", "title": "polarization"}], "description": "The class studies campaigns, polarization, agenda-setting, framing, and media trust."}, {"id": "17e26891-834c-4b51-b75c-09c5dd48f3b9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Media psychology and identity", "children": [{"id": "c4c864b6-be83-4de2-bef5-5fc6c734363d", "type": "concept", "title": "parasocial relationships"}, {"id": "14eccb4f-3406-4890-8126-447aee48b866", "type": "concept", "title": "identity formation"}, {"id": "8fd0ef2a-4a96-4a49-9939-64ded9ff7ad5", "type": "concept", "title": "mood management"}], "description": "Students examine how people use media for belonging, emotion, identity, and self-presentation."}, {"id": "cbd8aca0-462c-4de1-91f3-ec14f5ca01a5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Children, vulnerable audiences, and media literacy", "children": [{"id": "4e6fbe95-e543-44e8-9e94-f0e522d2dd9d", "type": "concept", "title": "children and media"}, {"id": "fcc411c0-9486-44c9-8987-8762be8a7054", "type": "concept", "title": "media literacy"}, {"id": "e29684d9-8890-4eca-8127-19205ca5dfd7", "type": "concept", "title": "civic education"}], "description": "Students consider developmental, educational, and civic approaches to media effects."}]}, {"id": "6316fbd9-7755-4d0b-8252-c553a83b10cb", "type": "topic", "title": "Media Law, Ethics, and Press Freedom", "description": "Students gain a first-year map of the legal and ethical standards that shape responsible journalism and communication work.", "children": [{"id": "b67fe8c9-89e1-4f99-9aab-84f33d65f2ba", "type": "subtopic", "ti