veillance, source protection, and journalist safety."}]}, {"id": "2e00aa1e-0756-41ba-a04d-5296456780ff", "type": "topic", "title": "Representation, Diversity, and Global Media Systems", "description": "Students learn to analyze whose voices are amplified, whose are excluded, and how media systems differ across cultures, nations, and communities.", "children": [{"id": "bac705b0-8116-4119-9baa-4c2b51fb7a55", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Representation and stereotyping", "children": [{"id": "399f3ced-850e-46bd-aa6b-b8122c007520", "type": "concept", "title": "symbolic annihilation"}, {"id": "ca5dc654-2065-494d-b133-3d58a8ef537b", "type": "concept", "title": "stereotypes"}, {"id": "00ba4168-fac3-44e2-956d-04dc14cbc30f", "type": "concept", "title": "intersectionality"}], "description": "Students examine how race, gender, class, disability, religion, sexuality, and nationality appear in media narratives."}, {"id": "c438ef13-09c0-4c78-b890-f7e73ff0cffe", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Newsroom diversity and source diversity", "children": [{"id": "37fa1c9a-e9b9-4078-ad20-0703f9c07d6e", "type": "concept", "title": "source audits"}, {"id": "2040d745-493b-4eb8-86a3-aac0220d322c", "type": "concept", "title": "community listening"}, {"id": "6f77e4e3-0c2b-4d74-814c-c39376cebfb6", "type": "concept", "title": "inclusive editing"}], "description": "The course connects inclusive journalism to accuracy, trust, community knowledge, and editorial blind spots."}, {"id": "434b0803-549c-456f-9204-711e06764343", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Global media systems", "children": [{"id": "85a1855d-96f3-4138-9119-ba08a6d07a07", "type": "concept", "title": "public service broadcasting"}, {"id": "e40f83d9-72ed-48d0-8296-34763393f2df", "type": "concept", "title": "state media"}, {"id": "0d70d1b6-8f09-41d7-bb5b-2436c5651943", "type": "concept", "title": "transnational media"}], "description": "Students compare commercial, public-service, state-controlled, and hybrid media systems."}, {"id": "bcfb1540-5a3e-4504-bd13-9e81ffe915f4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Media, power, and social change", "children": [{"id": "22ca8028-6a21-4c15-a29e-dc606985dbf8", "type": "concept", "title": "activist media"}, {"id": "a55b4520-08aa-4b47-831b-7f6ab4d94f3d", "type": "concept", "title": "networked movements"}, {"id": "90ab32b8-da3a-479d-8c26-88253c743444", "type": "concept", "title": "media and democracy"}], "description": "Students study media roles in protest, social movements, democracy, authoritarianism, and cultural change."}]}, {"id": "1a89c2a8-83dc-4437-b12d-2009d9c10373", "type": "topic", "title": "Misinformation, Verification, and Media Literacy", "description": "This unit provides the habits needed to navigate polluted information environments with skepticism and care.", "children": [{"id": "77cb6024-7337-4c89-8660-071a25b46d8f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Information disorder", "children": [{"id": "91385ca7-b914-4dcb-a203-585e53525680", "type": "concept", "title": "false context"}, {"id": "aef285a3-0c90-43f5-a220-f72d5651c20d", "type": "concept", "title": "manipulated content"}, {"id": "cae6d19a-5548-4fe6-b284-1fa471dc61f0", "type": "concept", "title": "coordinated campaigns"}], "description": "Students distinguish misinformation, disinformation, malinformation, propaganda, rumor, satire, and error."}, {"id": "192c02ae-b9eb-4e52-ab4d-6f4810feb253", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Verification basics", "children": [{"id": "8035c596-2b83-4869-8c1c-cecb95bb461c", "type": "concept", "title": "lateral reading"}, {"id": "ea1bd8e0-89bc-4705-bda9-89ec1f937702", "type": "concept", "title": "reverse image search"}, {"id": "e7dd2f73-39b4-421a-bf75-2c6b8e405354", "type": "concept", "title": "source provenance"}], "description": "The course introduces lateral reading, source tracing, image search, geolocation clues, and claims checking."}, {"id": "134b1002-0e69-49a9-9281-05f7e6249f26", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Trust and credibility", "children": [{"id": "c008ea06-e856-48f3-9de4-9d9a0774f70a", "type": "concept", "title": "transparency"}, {"id": "7d934853-131d-4e24-86a8-bc3905a07403", "type": "concept", "title": "expertise"}, {"id": "37b58387-ba6c-4034-890b-fb805791f0d4", "type": "concept", "title": "institutional trust"}], "description": "Students analyze how audiences decide what to trust and how institutions earn or lose credibility."}, {"id": "d3fe3963-62f7-4fb3-8a0a-911c59d78ec9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Responsible sharing", "children": [{"id": "abb39afd-a516-4ff3-91cc-d4cd19c5b34b", "type": "concept", "title": "pause before sharing"}, {"id": "7133773d-4291-4c72-89de-14fca3b45945", "type": "concept", "title": "context checks"}, {"id": "95003ceb-bfe0-40e5-871e-67fc26710c3e", "type": "concept", "title": "correction behavior"}], "description": "Students learn practical habits for slowing down, checking claims, and avoiding amplification of harm."}]}, {"id": "c644f1e1-75b7-42d3-9917-75857ef5d812", "type": "topic", "title": "Careers in Communication and Professional Pathways", "description": "The final section helps students connect the survey to real careers while building a flexible sense of professional identity in a changing media field.", "children": [{"id": "deaa3eda-12ae-4e8e-88b1-6edc0058f2a2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Journalism roles", "children": [{"id": "a3ddf4ef-f077-4f95-929e-4b6f5ac3dee6", "type": "concept", "title": "reporter"}, {"id": "01bafd47-224c-4f29-8464-de52884d0be3", "type": "concept", "title": "editor"}, {"id": "68f324bb-73d1-4b44-baa2-0520aaf58477", "type": "concept", "title": "producer and audience roles"}], "description": "Students map reporting, editing, audience, data, product, visual, audio, video, and investigative pathways."}, {"id": "1fb427fb-ecc4-433a-b26c-48f4f26effc6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strategic and organizational communication roles", "children": [{"id": "e68495c7-c35e-49df-b6d6-a1a5f63d2be0", "type": "concept", "title": "PR specialist"}, {"id": "aadb96df-21ee-424f-8cc3-607